========================================================================================
PART A -- exact H-drift endpoint and length-weighted OCF formula
========================================================================================
identity: E[Delta H|T] = (a_(n-2)-(n-1)H)/C(n,2)
OCF form: E[Delta H|T] = 2*(K-nH)/C(n,2)
K = sum_I 2^(|I|+f_I) = 2^(n-1) sum_I prod_(C in I) 2^(2-|C|)
n=4 specialization: E[Delta H|T] = 2*(3-H)/3
n=5 specialization: E[Delta H|T] = (12-H-6*t5)/5
n=4: rows=8 H-fibres=3 split-fibres=0 {}
n=5: rows=64 H-fibres=7 split-fibres=1 {15: (Fraction(-21, 5), Fraction(-3, 1))}
n=6: rows=1024 H-fibres=19 split-fibres=5 {9: (Fraction(12, 5), Fraction(4, 1)), 15: (Fraction(12, 5), Fraction(4, 1)), 23: (Fraction(-4, 15), Fraction(4, 3)), 33: (Fraction(-4, 1), Fraction(-12, 5)), 37: (Fraction(-92, 15), Fraction(-68, 15))}
first H-only obstruction: n=5, H=15; t5=2 gives -3, t5=3 gives -21/5
proof: each Hamiltonian path is destroyed once for each of its n-1 arcs;
orders with one backward adjacency are created by flipping their unique bad arc.
THM-062 gives a_(n-2)=sum_I 2^|I|*(2^(f_I+1)-n-1),
while H=sum_I 2^|I|; subtraction gives the displayed OCF formula.
n=6 obstruction to pointwise mean reversion: E[H]=45/2 but H=23 has drift 4/3 or -4/15.

