ASSUMPTION CHALLENGE / TOURNAMENT ANALYSIS
drift vertices are odd-cycle collections and endpoint coefficients, not runners or raw arcs;
self-line vertices are ordinary-class equalities, kappa-lines, and free V4 orbits.
H alone destroys cycle-length occupancy; the converse-merged atlas destroys same-vs-converse.
No joint carrier tournament is formed: drift exactness and ordinary-class equality are different predicates.
Within the drift predicate, the exactness/compression carrier order is
length-weighted OCF K > endpoint pair (H,a_(n-2)) > direct flip ledger > H-only;
fingerprint: transitive score histogram {0:1,1:1,2:1,3:1}, cycles=0, SCCs=4, HP=1.

